  "result": "Quiz 0002 on O4 is written: `quizzes/0002.json` with its key in `keys/0002.json`. I answered each item from its stem alone to check there is one defensible answer, but I haven't had it checked any other way.\n\nIt has six items. Four are multiple choice, one is numeric and one is a short answer.\n- **q1:** who owns the control flow.\n- **q2:** classify the makerspace assistant's fixed-order design as a workflow or an agent.\n- **q3:** which task suits a fixed workflow.\n- **q4:** the extra cost of an agent over a workflow for 500 booking requests.\n- **q5:** say in one sentence who decides the next step in each.\n- **q6:** a stretch item on when an open-ended request calls for an agent, with a step limit to keep cost down.\n\nThis quiz comes before any lesson on O4. I wrote it from Anthropic's \"Building effective agents\", which defines workflows as predefined code paths and agents as the model directing its own process. I haven't added the source to `RESOURCES.md`.\n\nI used three new misconception ids, M7 to M9, and recorded them in `NOTES.md`:\n- **M7:** treating several model calls or tools as what makes something an agent.\n- **M8:** assuming an agent is best for everything.\n- **M9:** assuming a fixed workflow is best for everything.\n\nWould you like a short lesson on O4 before you take the quiz, or do you want to try the quiz cold first?",
